{"path":"atomic/atomic/wait","title":"std::atomic<T>::wait","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::atomic&lt;T&gt;::</span>wait","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/wait","section":"atomic","kind":"page","summary":"Performs atomic waiting operations. Behaves as if it repeatedly performs the following steps:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td><div><span id=\"Version_1\"></span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> wait<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T old, <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1)</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(constexpr since C++26)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> wait<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T old,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Performs atomic waiting operations. Behaves as if it repeatedly performs the following steps: \n</p>\n<ul><li> Compare the <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/object\">value representation</a> of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">this<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>load<span class=\"br0\">(</span>order<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> with that of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">old</span></code>.\n<ul><li> If those are equal, then blocks until <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> is notified by <span class=\"t-lc\">notify_one()</span> or <span class=\"t-lc\">notify_all()</span>, or the thread is unblocked spuriously.\n</li><li> Otherwise, returns.\n</li></ul>\n</li></ul>\n<p>These functions are guaranteed to return only if value has changed, even if underlying implementation unblocks spuriously.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code> is not <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2114\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_relaxed</span></span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2115\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_consume</span></span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2116\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_acquire</span></span></a></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a></span></code>, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> old\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the value to check the <code>atomic</code>'s object no longer contains\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> order\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> memory order constraints to enforce\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This form of change-detection is often more efficient than simple polling or pure spinlocks.\n</p><p>Due to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ABA_problem\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">ABA problem</a>, transient changes from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">old</span></code> to another value and back to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">old</span></code> might be missed, and not unblock.\n</p><p>The comparison is bitwise (similar to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/memcmp\">std::memcmp</a></span>); no comparison operator is used. Padding bits that never participate in an object's value representation are ignored.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;atomic&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;chrono&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;future&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;thread&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">literals</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic\"><span class=\"kw2083\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> all_tasks_completed<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic\"><span class=\"kw2083\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> completion_count<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future\"><span class=\"kw2201\">std::<span class=\"me2\">future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> task_futures<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">16</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic\"><span class=\"kw2083\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> outstanding_task_count<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">16</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// Spawn several tasks which take different amounts of</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// time, then decrement the outstanding task count.</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future\"><span class=\"kw2201\">std::<span class=\"me2\">future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> task_future <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> task_futures<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        task_future <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/async\"><span class=\"kw2204\">std::<span class=\"me2\">async</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"co1\">// This sleep represents doing real work...</span>\n            <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/sleep_for\"><span class=\"kw2170\">std::<span class=\"me2\">this_thread</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sleep_for</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>50ms<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n            <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>completion_count<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"sy2\">--</span>outstanding_task_count<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n            <span class=\"co1\">// When the task count falls to zero, notify</span>\n            <span class=\"co1\">// the waiter (main thread in this case).</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>outstanding_task_count.<span class=\"me1\">load</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                all_tasks_completed <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                all_tasks_completed.<span class=\"me1\">notify_one</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    all_tasks_completed.<span class=\"me1\">wait</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Tasks completed = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> completion_count.<span class=\"me1\">load</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Tasks completed = 16</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/notify_one\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>notify_one</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  notifies at least one thread waiting on the atomic object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/notify_all\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>notify_all</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  notifies all threads blocked waiting on the atomic object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_notify_one\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atomic_notify_one</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  notifies a thread blocked in atomic_wait <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_notify_all\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atomic_notify_all</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  notifies all threads blocked in atomic_wait <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"atomic","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"atomic/atomic","title":"std::atomic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::atomic<T>::wait","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Performs atomic waiting operations. Behaves as if it repeatedly performs the following steps:"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"old, order"},{"label":"Notes","note":"This form of change-detection is often more efficient than simple polling or pure spinlocks."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"notify_one","note":"notifies at least one thread waiting on the atomic object"},{"label":"notify_all","note":"notifies all threads blocked waiting on the atomic object"},{"label":"atomic_notify_one","note":"notifies a thread blocked in atomic_wait"},{"label":"atomic_notify_all","note":"notifies all threads blocked in atomic_wait"}]}]},"standards":["C++20","C++26"],"wordCount":341,"codeBlockCount":2}
